<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Szlachta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The szlachta was the hereditary noble class of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and later of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. Unusually numerous, it enjoyed extensive privileges, including the right to elect the king and to participate in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>. Accounts of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth describe the szlachta as the political nation of the state, whose liberties shaped its distinctive system of noble democracy but also contributed to governmental paralysis.</p></div>
